  "body": "Stacked on #981 (on #961). Fork synced at v0.18.0.\n\n## What changed\n\n`assets/posts/fanuc-lathe.cps` now writes an inch document as an inch program instead of refusing it. It declares `programUnits = \"mm inch\"` and reads `postOptions.Units`. The stream and every geometry or refusal check stay in mm; values are converted only in the word formatters:\n\n| Word | G21 (unchanged) | G20 (new) |\n|---|---|---|\n| X (diameter), Z, I K, G76 first-block R, tool note D/R | mm, 3 dp | in, 4 dp |\n| G99 F (feed per rev) | mm/rev, 4 dp | in/rev, 4 dp |\n| G32 / G76 F (lead) | mm, 4 dp | in, 6 dp |\n| G76 P(k) Q(dmin) Q(1st), G83 Q (no-point increments) | whole microns | whole 0.0001 in |\n| G96 S | m/min | ft/min (m/min / 0.3048) |\n| G97 S, G50 S, G83 P dwell, G76 P(m)(r)(a) | unchanged | unchanged |\n| PART LOAD advance comment | `ADVANCE 30` | `ADVANCE 1.1811 IN` |\n\n**Refused by name, never guessed:**\n- A C-axis live-tool section on an inch program. Its feed is a composite rate that counts degrees as the linear unit, and how that rate works under G20 was not confirmed from a public source.\n- A per-rev feed that rounds to `F0` at the program's digits.\n- A G76 depth smaller than one least increment.\n\n`program_units` drops Fanuc Lathe from its mm-only list, and `assets/posts/AGENTS.md` says the same. The decisions are in `docs/decisions/977-fanuc-lathe-inch.md`.\n\n## Sources (public, behaviour only)\n- RS-274 / ISO 6983 for G20 / G21.\n- The public Fanuc 0i-T lathe programming vocabulary the post was already specced from: G96 / G97 / G50, G99, and the two-block G76 with P / Q as no-point counts of the least input increment (0.001 mm, or 0.0001 in under inch input).\n- Published lathe programming guides with inch two-line G76 examples that use four-digit P / Q in 0.0001 in.\n\nNo vendor post, Fusion or HSMWorks material was used.\n\n## How tested\n- New suite `lathe_post_inch` (fixtures in `tests/fanuc_lathe_inch/`):\n  - `every_turning_stream_posts_the_mm_program_in_inches`: covers facing, profile rough + finish, groove + part, axial drill, the G76 thread and the G32 thread. Each mm post must match its committed mm golden byte for byte, and Units mm must post exactly what no unit posts. Each inch program is checked word by word against its mm twin (lengths / 25.4, feeds / 25.4, increments / 2.54, SFM = m/min x 3.28084, everything else equal, G20 before any motion, no G21). The inch programs are committed under `golden/nc/inch/fanuc-lathe/`.\n  - `the_inch_thread_words_are_pinned`: `G76 P010000 Q157 R0` / `G76 X0.378 Z0.315 P472 Q157 F0.07874`, plus the G32 lead `F0.07874`.\n  - `an_inch_document_posts_inch_through_the_gate`: SetUnits inch, then `post_setup` gives the same program as the engine.\n  - `surface_speed_is_feet_per_minute_and_rpm_never_scales`: `G96 S656` from 200 m/min, with `G50 S12000` unchanged.\n  - `a_peck_counts_the_inch_increment`: `G83 ... Q394 P500`.\n  - `what_inch_cannot_say_soundly_is_refused_by_name`.\n- I also ran these suites by hand, all green: lathe_post, lathe_post_g76, lathe_post_refusals, program_units, mcp_units, c_axis_live, c_axis_unwind, lathe_post_tormach, lathe_spindle_law, lathe_blade_corner, lathe_nose_tip, coolant_followups, comment_escape, conformance, inverted_post, control_comp, wear_comp, program_entry, and every turning* suite.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/issue/902-document-units` (the new golden dir makes it run every app suite): green on 8e26be0c (all app suites, 12.9 min); clippy `-D warnings` clean on the new suite and program_units.\n- No existing golden moved.\n\n## Not exercised\n- No real control. The inch digits (4 dp lengths and per-rev feeds, 6 dp leads, 0.0001 in increments) follow the published inch least increment and have not been proved on a 0i-T.\n- Rounding per-rev feeds to 4 dp in inch is coarse on very small feeds: 0.0267 mm/rev posts as F0.001, about 5% low. That is a slower cut, never a faster one; see the decision file.\n- C-axis live tooling in inch is refused, not converted.\n\nChangelog: Fanuc Lathe post writes inch programs (G20; X/Z in inches, G99 in/rev, G96 in surface feet per minute, G76/G83 increments in 0.0001 in) for an inch document instead of refusing it; C-axis live tooling stays mm-only\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #977\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
